Receipt recovery and ordinary message history need independently polled scopes
inside their existing delivery owner. Serial receipt-first ordering merely
reverses a dependency: a held receipt query must not prevent a fresh original
from arriving. An early empty control round can precede creation of the new
receipt; preserve bounded post-original recovery before parking exact custody
as quiet. Preserve the immediate best-effort flush's payload-custody-before-control
ordering; that caller must not start a control exchange after its payload fails.
Retained automatic recovery independently polls receipt-eligible originals,
including manifest cards whose bytes still await recipient consent. Card receipt,
download consent and complete-file custody remain distinct evidence.
Keep both recovery scopes under the same cancellation/deadline owner, without
retaining store guards or increasing TCP capacity. The real inbound-only
[receipt-scope regressions](../crates/mesh-talk-core/src/node/delivery_runtime_tests.rs)
require a genuine pre-existing authenticated receipt through held ordinary
history, fresh plaintext through held control history without false Delivered,
and first-send confirmation after a deliberately early empty control round.

Do not encode failed, unchanged and completed work as one empty-result boolean

Receipt-control and ordinary DM-history scopes progress concurrently within the
existing retained-destination recovery owner, so either scope may complete while the other
is blocked. Only exact authenticated recipient receipts establish Delivered;
ordinary Have and opaque relay custody remain separate evidence. An empty early
receipt round cannot settle a fresh send: after positive original custody, retain
the existing bounded post-original control pull while that exact work remains.
Immediate best-effort flush retains payload-custody-before-control ordering,
including file offers: a failed payload cannot start a receipt-control exchange.
Retained automatic recovery independently polls all receipt-eligible originals,
including genuine manifest cards with unavailable bytes and pending consent.
Own-account copies and receipt transfers do not add a parallel receipt query.

One eligible retained destination can own two direct scope exchanges, plus its existing
relay alternative (at most two simultaneous offices from a four-candidate batch).
The one verified-peer reconciliation owner polls two distinct direct scopes
alongside its existing serial relay lane. Both relay calls drain the same
pairwise mailbox and retain their separate subsequent local projections; they
are not duplicated concurrently. Each relay pull visits its existing
at-most-four office candidates serially, not a new parallel fanout. Route racing still admits at most two candidates per dial, and all these
owners share the unchanged eight total/seven outbound TCP slots and admission
waits. No new producer, durable queue, timer or independent deadline is added;
actual connections retain their permits until retirement. These are concurrency
bounds, not guarantees of progress while unrelated owners exhaust capacity.

